DEVLOG — updates.txt second pass (b2bc765..628f9fa)

Worked through static/updates.txt. Items shipped: hero two-line identity
block, /pictures + /writings coming-soon routes, white navbar pill, even
card halo, experience-card alignment + contrasting dark palette, Lichess
challenge box, git-notes dev log, font sampler at /fonts-lab (pending a
pick).

TWO THINGS THAT WERE NOT IN THE FILE BUT MATTERED MORE:

1. static/updates.txt was being PUBLISHED. Everything in static/ is copied
   into the deploy output; it landed at build/updates.txt and Netlify would
   have served it at akhilgogineni.lol/updates.txt. The file containing the
   request for a log 'not visible to public eye' was itself public. It is
   gitignored, which is exactly why this was easy to miss — untracked says
   nothing about whether something ships. Moved to the repo root, where the
   same ignore rule still covers it. No git diff exists for this because the
   file was never tracked, which is why it is recorded here.

2. Prerendering has never actually run. No route sets
   'export const prerender = true' and SvelteKit 1 defaults it to false, so
   'prerender: { entries: [...] }' has been inert since before this work.
   Every page is rendered on demand by the Netlify function; the build emits
   no HTML at all (find build -name '*.html' is empty). I had claimed the
   opposite while planning the new routes. The entries list stays because it
   would matter the moment prerendering is enabled.

MEASUREMENT NOTE: fps numbers taken during this pass are unreliable. The
machine was loaded enough that the unchanged committed BackgroundGradient
also dropped from ~52 to ~23 between runs. Comparisons here were done as
interleaved A/B rather than as before/after readings, and the halo change
measured at parity. Re-baseline on a quiet machine before trusting any
absolute number.
